{"plan_json": "{
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "objective": "Research NFPA 484/652/654 requirements for frequency of emptying dust collection containers — is 'daily' a hard requirement or based on accumulation thresholds? What applies to low-duty research labs?",
      "rationale": "The user needs to know if daily emptying is a quantitative requirement or if a fill-level/time threshold is defensible for a lab generating only tens of grams per week.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "objective": "Research NFPA 484/652 requirements for interim storage containers for reactive metal fines — is a dedicated grounded steel pail required, or can an existing EHS waste container (HDPE/fiber drum) be used?",
      "rationale": "The user needs to know if the intermediate steel pail is a hard NFPA requirement, best practice, or DHA-dependent, and whether non-conductive EHS containers are acceptable.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "objective": "Identify and attempt to verify specific Uline SKUs for carbon-loaded conductive polyethylene bags/liners meeting the user's specifications (≤10⁶ Ω/sq, carbon-loaded, 3-4 mil, ~15x18 or larger)",
      "rationale": "The user specifically requests verified Uline product page URLs with part numbers and pricing for conductive PE liners.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "objective": "Identify and attempt to verify specific Uline SKUs for grounded steel pails with tight-fitting lids suitable for interim storage of reactive metal fines (≤$100)",
      "rationale": "If a separate grounded steel pail is needed, the user wants specific commercially available products with Uline part numbers.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "objective": "Cross-reference alternative suppliers (Protective Packaging Corp, Daubert Cromwell, International Plastics, McMaster-Carr) for conductive PE liners if Uline SKUs cannot be verified",
      "rationale": "Fallback sourcing if Uline verification fails.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "objective": "Compile final answer with all practical recommendations, verified product links where possible, and honest disclosure where URLs cannot be verified",
      "rationale": "The user explicitly requires honesty about URL verification status.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    }
  ]
}"}

{"plan_json": "{
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "objective": "Research NFPA 484/652/654 and peer-reviewed literature on liner removal procedures for combustible metal dust — settling time, operator grounding, sealing techniques, and aerosolization prevention",
      "rationale": "Step 1 of the SOP requires exact procedures for removing a conductive liner from a vacuum bin without creating dust clouds or breaking grounding chains.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "objective": "Research passivation of fine aluminum-alloy (AlSi10Mg) powder — mineral oil coating, inert containment alternatives, hydrogen hazard from water, and disposal classification impacts",
      "rationale": "Step 2 asks whether chemical passivation is needed/recommended, with specific evaluation of mineral oil vs dry sealed containment for low-quantity lab scenarios.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "objective": "Research interim storage requirements for reactive metal fines — max fill, inerting, moisture exclusion, labeling, segregation from incompatibles",
      "rationale": "Step 3 needs specific guidance on how to store sealed liners in the grounded steel interim pail.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "objective": "Research RCRA classification of aluminum and silicon powder waste, hazardous waste labeling, and transfer procedures to EHS disposal containers",
      "rationale": "Step 4 needs RCRA D001 ignitable/reactive considerations and coordination guidance for university EHS.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "objective": "Research cross-contamination and thermite/galvanic incompatibility risks between mixed reactive metal powders (Al + Fe oxide, Al + other metals), and whether dedicated containers are needed per metal type",
      "rationale": "Steps 5-6 ask about switching metals and the risks of mixing different metal powders.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "objective": "Research vacuum cleaning/purging procedures between powder types — dry wipe vs damp wipe, filter replacement cadence, prohibition on water with aluminum, ground continuity re-verification",
      "rationale": "Step 7 needs a safe cleaning method for the vacuum interior including filters, hose, bin.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "objective": "Compile the complete SOP with master checklist, PPE requirements, Class D extinguisher placement, prohibitions list, and all citations",
      "rationale": "Final deliverable must be a single authoritative document suitable for a student operator.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    }
  ]
}"}

{"plan_json": "{
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "objective": "Research anodized aluminum dielectric properties — surface resistivity, dielectric strength, thickness of sulfuric (clear) anodize, and whether a low-voltage DMM can punch through it",
      "rationale": "Claim 1 asks whether the OL/megohm reading is diagnostic of an engineered dielectric (anodize) vs native oxide or oil film. Need hard numbers on anodize resistivity and breakdown voltage.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "objective": "Research whether anodizing of aluminum vacuum tools/nozzles is standard practice in EXP-certified equipment, and whether Nilfisk P/N 01768900 documentation exists for finish specification",
      "rationale": "Claim 2 asks whether clear anodize is the most likely explanation for the symptom set.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "objective": "Research NFPA 77/484 isolated-conductor hazard and propagating brush discharge threshold for coated/anodized metals — is an anodized tool over grounded metal an ignition concern?",
      "rationale": "Claim 3 asks whether the hazard is resolved once the tool body is bonded to ground through a clean joint, and whether the anodize layer itself poses a PBD risk.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "objective": "Research UL 1213 par. 22 ground-continuity requirements, reconcile with NFPA 77 bonding criteria, and address whether a 4-ohm conductive hose violates 0.1-ohm-per-connection",
      "rationale": "Claim 4 asks for the governing pass/fail criterion and reconciliation between the strict OEM manual and permissive NFPA 77 figures.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "objective": "Determine correct remediation approach — bond the joint vs strip the tool vs replace — and address certification/alteration concerns",
      "rationale": "Claim 5 asks for the practical fix and whether it constitutes an alteration that nullifies certification.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "objective": "Address safety of the diagnostic abrasion itself (aluminum grinding dust hazard) and identify any omissions",
      "rationale": "Claim 6 and the omissions section.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "objective": "Compile final answer with verdicts for all 6 claims plus omissions, with citations",
      "rationale": "Final deliverable.",
      "status": "pending",
      "result": null,
      "evaluation": null
    }
  ]
}"}

